## Re-export Strategies

### Pattern 1: Flatten Hierarchy

```xiom
mod net {
  mod protocol {
    mod tcp {
      pub fn connect(addr: Str) -> Bool { true }
      pub fn send(data: Str) { }
      pub fn disconnect() { }
    }
  }

  // Flatten to clean API
  pub use protocol::tcp::connect;
  pub use protocol::tcp::send;
  pub use protocol::tcp::disconnect;
}
```

Users see: `net.connect()`, `net.send()`, `net.disconnect()` — no deep paths.

### Pattern 2: Selective Exposure

```xiom
mod database {
  mod internal {
    pub fn raw_query(sql: Str) -> Str { "result" }
    pub fn raw_execute(sql: Str) { }
  }

  mod public_api {
    pub fn find_user(id: Int) -> Str { "user" }
    pub fn list_all() -> Str { "all users" }
  }

  // Only expose safe, curated API
  pub use public_api::find_user;
  pub use public_api::list_all;
  // Never expose internal::raw_query — it's dangerous!
}
```

### Pattern 3: Renaming Conflicts

```xiom
mod graphics {
  mod shapes {
    pub fn draw() { }
  }
  mod colors {
    pub fn draw() { }
  }

  pub use shapes::draw as draw_shape;
  pub use colors::draw as draw_color;
}
```

